commit 895332928cc939f9fc0b53b8b4cd4684cfce5133
Author: Saikrishna Edupuganti <6157640+krsna1729@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 18 15:18:07 2026 +0200

    fix(protocol): close Robotweax differential correctness gaps
    
    Protocol-correctness hardening pass against the Robotweax differential
    reference and pinned Haivision libsrt, from the merged #118 base
    (ee2faab). No capacity claims, no API surface change for embedders.
    
    - Receive-window credit is an absolute 31-bit boundary
      (ack_seq + advertised_free), moved only by a current Small/Full ACK and
      capped by the handshake-negotiated window, so a Light ACK can no longer
      recycle stale credit. The peer's advertised flight-flag size now bounds
      the sender too.
    - A zero receive window reopens with an immediate Full ACK when the
      application frees buffer, coalesced across a burst of releases.
    - Peer liveness is refreshed only after a packet passes its own semantic
      or authentication validation; malformed control input and
      unauthenticated DATA are rejected before any state change.
    - Peer SHUTDOWN is terminal-pending: buffered DATA keeps its TSBPD
      deadline, and the terminal event waits for the receive path and the
      application queue to drain.
    - TLPKTDROP keeps bounded sequence tombstones (media released) so a
      repeated NAK is answered with DROPREQ again until the cumulative ACK.
    - NAK processing is all-or-none: the whole report is validated against
      the retained window before anything is queued, and the parser no longer
      truncates dense ranges.
    - Encrypted retransmission reuses the first transmission's crypto stamp,
      reproducing its protected bytes under the same key generation, and a
      generation cannot be retired while a retained packet depends on it.
    
    docs/differential-audit-robotweax.md records the reference revisions,
    the per-item decisions, the deliberate divergences, and the evidence.

